uid":"b37a99a9-b98a-4e1e-8499-322d717f8e2b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2aee-e1eb-4e4a-4c27"},{"link_uuid":"c078638d-718d-428c-9edd-70dae3b1f0a9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8d9c-8aa9-0886-4a6c"},{"link_uuid":"76afba33-ee76-477d-9b55-81dbdb48b247","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ff33-19cb-b5c7-4cbb"},{"link_uuid":"b33ba454-d777-4295-8c0e-be6e84c84520","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c0c0-c44b-4722-4d89"},{"link_uuid":"7cdf4c4f-9805-489e-8e78-e6d34be7b65b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"01f2-8e34-e02d-4a4e"},{"link_uuid":"6120e2e9-397f-4185-b6b9-7ba9f6e79ad6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f12c-f6f4-2230-4237"},{"link_uuid":"ece1495f-35e4-4bf5-9520-5db2fc5b43d0","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fdc7-253b-34af-417c"},{"link_uuid":"ad87f1a3-23d8-425a-b773-37cad6245835","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6ad4-a8db-9beb-4d42"},{"link_uuid":"9b39e2cd-c0c5-4975-a648-8fcd1d47e675","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2a2f-3ef0-a2e5-4609"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit/workflow cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96.py:1-13` — Preserve mutually exclusive availability/input-rejection signals and fail-closed outcome. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_midrun_fail_closed.py:1-17, 117-119, 138-145, 202-207` — Preserve raw batch-error propagation, plan-review degradation, sidecar ordering, and defensive code-review contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_insufficient_evidence_marker.py:1-10, 333-335, 498-512` — Preserve insufficiency versus refutation, retryable disposition, and anti-misclassification guidance. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_lint.py:75-78, 95-98` — Preserve `batch.when` reference checking and `patternProperties` support. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_map_fanout.py:123-136` — Preserve one concise concurrency discriminator. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py:1-14` — Preserve per-call aggregation and sidecar exposure. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_warmup.py:1-17, 48-52` — Preserve warm-before-fan-out eligibility, fallback, and cache read/write observation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_assemble_memo.py:1-13, 115-120, 147-149` — Preserve run-scoped keying, identical context, and exact `2+K` cost. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_hierarchy_incomplete.py:1-14` — Preserve bounded retry, incomplete-detail values, and INDETERMINATE propagation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_live_plumbing.py:1-11, 38-41` — Preserve execution through `RunnerAgentStep` and provision of required prompt variables. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_metrics.py:1-11` — Preserve workflow duration split, LLM-call proxy, and sidecar lifting. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_verify_recovery.py:1-11, 90-103, 266-271` — Preserve scaled budgets, findings recovery, and loud step-ID validation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_workflow.py:1-17, 372-377, 450-455` — Preserve offline end-to-end shape, DET short-circuit, lossless sidecar, and verdict operations. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_production_batch_runner.py:1-9, 241-245` — Preserve behavioral equivalence, sizing behavior, and journaled plan parity. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py:160-168, 229-234, 285-289` — Preserve environment-safe redispatch, benign disabled-workflow handling, and elapsed-time pacing. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_review_output_budget.py:1-22, 198-201` — Preserve resolved-model maximum as the floor and per-request clamp semantics. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_review_skeleton.py:1-11` — Preserve offline four-pass execution, trace capture, and nested prompt validation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_snapshot_stream_bounds_093a.py:1-37, 218-223, 321-326` — Preserve timeout, concurrent stderr drain, closed stdin, stall abort, cleanup, and credential redaction. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96.py tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_midrun_fail_closed.py tests/unit/workflow/test_insufficient_evidence_marker.py tests/unit/workflow/test_lint.py tests/unit/workflow/test_map_fanout.py tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_warmup.py tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_assemble_memo.py tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_hierarchy_incomplete.py tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_re